(all laughs)

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.850
- I know I haven't put yogurt on today.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.281
(audience applauds)

00:00:21.281 --> 00:00:23.370
- Well, I have to say we all know that,

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.548
and Great Britain lost Queen Elizabeth.

00:00:25.548 --> 00:00:26.381
- [Sarah] Oh.

00:00:26.381 --> 00:00:27.510
- So, and that was last year.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.300
So, what are some of
your fondest memories?

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.890
- Well, actually right
now, it would be that

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.210
in coming towards the
end, she never was able

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.950
to walk her doggies, her corgis.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:38.783
- Yeah.
(audience groans sadly)

00:00:38.783 --> 00:00:40.290
- And so, I know it's so sad.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.870
And I used to go into the favorite place

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:45.630
where she used to walk and take a video,

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.340
and say, oh, and you'd love this,

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.610
look, the magnolia's coming
out and the snow drops are out

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:50.935
(audience coos)
and the primroses are out.

00:00:50.935 --> 00:00:52.220
- [Kelly] Oh, I love that.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:55.680
- And so, and I just did
that walk before I came here,

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.660
and I got really teared up actually,

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.310
because I thought, oh,
I'll just send it to her.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:00.589
Oh no, she's not there.

00:01:00.589 --> 00:01:01.929
And she was such an

00:01:01.929 --> 00:01:02.762
extraordinary lady.
- That's the thing

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.595
with people passing,

00:01:03.595 --> 00:01:05.700
you're like it hits you at weird times.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.220
- Yeah, but one of the
things she'd say now,

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.990
to me, to come on this show,

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:13.020
she'd say, "Go on, get out
there, keep being yourself."

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:13.950
That's what she always used

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.000
to say to me.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.590
- And I think, think that's the secret

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.910
why I just keep coming back
rather like a, I don't know,

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.689
something you put on flowers,

00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:23.700
(audience applauds)
I just keep coming back.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.950
I was gonna say something
else and stopped.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.750
- Is this true that you and Princess Di

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.160
once dressed as policewomen?

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.200
Like for a, was it a bachelorette party?

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.790
- Well, it was my hen
party actually, 1986.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:34.530
- [Kelly] OK, oh, is that what
you call them hen parties?

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:35.363
- [Sarah] Yes.

00:01:35.363 --> 00:01:37.140
- [Kelly] (laughs) I love
that, I didn't know that.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.010
- [Sarah] Yeah.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.180
- [Kelly] I love this!

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.520
- But you know, it was extraordinary,

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.200
because we went to a nightclub.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.660
Of course you go to a nightclub
with the Princess of Wales,

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.108
then Princess of Wales.

00:01:47.108 --> 00:01:50.820
And I was just still
Fergie, wasn't married yet.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.120
And we went into this
nightclub and she was very good

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:55.230
as her costume.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.540
Anyway, so we sat down (chuckles),

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.520
and the waiter came up to
us and said, "Excuse me,

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.920
this is a member's club and it's for fun,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.211
and we don't serve police officers here."

00:02:04.211 --> 00:02:05.044
(audience laugh)

00:02:05.044 --> 00:02:06.300
Looking straight at us.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.290
- They thought you were real

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.400
police officers, A.
- Yes.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.100
- And then two, they
kicked police officers out.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:16.100
- Yes, and we went out and
as we came out of the stairs,

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.569
a lady was getting out of a cab,

00:02:18.569 --> 00:02:20.970
and Diana said, "She's got my dress on."

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.685
I said, "Dutch!", I called her Dutch.

00:02:22.685 --> 00:02:24.690
I said, "Dutch, no, no,
no, you can't say that,

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:26.280
we're meant to be police officers."

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.843
It was very funny, and then we were.

00:02:27.843 --> 00:02:28.988
- Keep in character!

00:02:28.988 --> 00:02:29.821
(all laugh)

00:02:29.821 --> 00:02:31.940
- But Kelly, we were then arrested.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.282
(all laugh)

00:02:34.282 --> 00:02:36.600
- I missed this story, what?

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.509
- We were arrested by Parks police.

00:02:39.509 --> 00:02:41.730
So we got in the back of the van.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:42.780
- What did you do to get arrested?

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.120
- She had put her engagement
ring round the other way,

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.230
and I put mine round the other way.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.000
And we were sitting in there like this,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.870
and she just looked around and
saw a smokey bacon flavored

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.107
crisps and started taking
them and eating them,

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:57.330
and the policeman in the front
said, "You can't do that."

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.200
We were.
- Just Did.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.033
- Just did

00:02:59.033 --> 00:02:59.866
- [Kelly] Just did.

00:02:59.866 --> 00:03:01.770
- Yeah, and then eventually they realized

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:05.752
that it was Diana and me.

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:09.660
- But wait, why did y'all get arrested?

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.225
- Oh, well 'cause we were
impersonating police officers.

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.880
(all laugh)

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.150
- [Kelly] Oh my god, people
are allowed to be in costume.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:18.983
- Hello?

00:03:18.983 --> 00:03:20.272
- Yeah.
- Anyway, but.

00:03:20.272 --> 00:03:21.192
- Uh, hello?

00:03:21.192 --> 00:03:22.025
(all laugh)

00:03:22.025 --> 00:03:23.268
- I'm in jury.

00:03:23.268 --> 00:03:25.864
- I love you, that's incredible.

00:03:25.864 --> 00:03:26.910
- Incredible.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:27.743
- Oh my god.

00:03:27.743 --> 00:03:28.860
- And of course, everyone
always says to me,

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:31.830
but you must miss Dutch, you and Diana.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:35.610
And I go, no, 'cause I
mean, she's with me all day.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.260
'Cause she's the only one who really,

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.769
she and I, we laughed a lot.

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:40.680
We got into trouble a lot.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.870
And then she used to, do you
know what she used to do?

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.529
She used to tell me the
worst story, joke story

00:03:45.529 --> 00:03:47.788
just before I had to be serious.

00:03:47.788 --> 00:03:49.860
(all laugh)

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.280
So I'd go straight in to
dinner, and she'd always,

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.050
'cause she'd been there
a few years before me.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.600
She used to run like a gazelle
to get into the dining room

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.433
quicker than me.

00:03:58.433 --> 00:04:00.360
And I now I thought, well
that's a bit strange.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.740
And when I got in I realized why,

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:02.970
'cause she got the young people,

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.628
and I got all the old people.

00:04:04.628 --> 00:04:05.837
- A clever one.

00:04:05.837 --> 00:04:07.607
So wait, your new book,
let's talk about it.

00:04:07.607 --> 00:04:08.440
- [Sarah] Oh yes.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.020
- So it's called "A Most Intriguing Lady".

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:10.853
- [Sarah] Yes.

00:04:10.853 --> 00:04:12.213
- So why did you, this is book two, is it?

00:04:12.213 --> 00:04:13.410
- Yes, book two.
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:14.490
- Just very quickly.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.078
- 'Cause I know you're so busy.

00:04:16.078 --> 00:04:20.753
I honestly, the British
newspapers and various newspapers

00:04:20.753 --> 00:04:23.302
around the world always like, I dunno why,

00:04:23.302 --> 00:04:26.104
they just love bad Fergie,
sells a lot of papers.

00:04:26.104 --> 00:04:26.937
(all laugh)

00:04:26.937 --> 00:04:31.080
- So I'm excited, I decided
that I'm still alive,

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.460
actually miracle, right?

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:36.000
So I thought that I
ought to really work out,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.130
it must be my red-headed
gene, that I was born

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.770
with bright red, a bath hat of red curls.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:42.843
I mean, what a joke, really?

00:04:42.843 --> 00:04:43.920
- Or beautiful.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.780
- Well, I researched all the redheads

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.930
and I believe every
woman, of course, and men,

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.674
but should be given a voice,

00:04:50.674 --> 00:04:54.570
and be respected and allowed
to be themselves, not judged.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:57.540
And I feel really strongly
that I then went back

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.345
into my ancestors and I found two redheads

00:05:00.345 --> 00:05:02.670
that have been in the grave,
and they'd all written

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:04.800
about the brothers but not about them.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.400
And that were my aunt, my
great-aunt, this is my great-aunt.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.233
- Oh wow.

00:05:09.233 --> 00:05:10.920
- And so I took her outta
the grave and I said,

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.600
come on darling, you are fabulous.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.820
Let's make a story about
you 'cause I'm alive

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:17.190
and you are my ancestor,
so I'm gonna write a novel,

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.870
but it's based on me, really.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:19.770
- Yeah, I love that.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:20.610
- [Sarah] And also, yeah.
(audience applauds)

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:22.837
- It's fun, yeah, (laughs) oh my God.

00:05:22.837 --> 00:05:24.240
- And also, guess what?

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.529
I actually, yeah, you can
star in it, we'll cast you.

00:05:26.529 --> 00:05:28.796
- Please, I would love
to, I do a great accent.

00:05:28.796 --> 00:05:29.873
- And you can sing the theme song.

00:05:29.873 --> 00:05:31.800
- Yeah, I was like, don't ask me to act.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.200
- But what I love about this book,

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.590
is that it's during the
day, she's very proper

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:39.392
and a lady, and everybody is.

00:05:39.392 --> 00:05:42.600
it's sort of Cary Grant "To
Catch a Thief" type bit.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:46.230
Yeah, and at night she
turns into a crimes,

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:47.340
a solving crimes.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:48.253
- [Kelly] Kinda like a detective.

00:05:48.253 --> 00:05:49.530
- She's a female detective!
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:50.363
Yeah, I love this.

00:05:50.363 --> 00:05:51.900
- And so it's very most intriguing.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:52.733
Yeah, you'll like it.

00:05:52.733 --> 00:05:53.566
- I like a mystery, I like, yeah.

00:05:53.566 --> 00:05:54.399
- I do too.

00:05:54.399 --> 00:05:55.295
- It's very sort of.

00:05:55.295 --> 00:05:56.409
- I didn't used to, but like lately,

00:05:56.409 --> 00:05:58.517
the past sort of five years
I'm like really into it.

00:05:58.517 --> 00:05:59.490
- [Sarah] Yep, I love it.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:00.540
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- [Sarah] I love it.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.790
- Okay, we have to do another
commercial break, y'all.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:05.640
But the Duchess's book is
called "A Most Intriguing Lady".

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:06.513
It's out now.

